# Every change needs a review from the owner.
#
# This repository publishes real cryptographic operations and makes factual
# claims about a NIST standard, so the paths below are called out explicitly
# rather than relying on the catch-all: a wrong number in a parameter table or a
# quietly weakened CSP is as much a defect here as a broken signature.

* @systemslibrarian

# The cryptographic path and its evidence.
/src/crypto/                    @systemslibrarian
/src/bench/                     @systemslibrarian
/vectors/                       @systemslibrarian
/src/__tests__/                 @systemslibrarian

# Claims about the standard. A wrong parameter or an uncited assertion is a
# defect, not a typo.
/src/data/                      @systemslibrarian
/src/ui/provenance.ts           @systemslibrarian
/src/ui/parameter-table.ts      @systemslibrarian
/src/ui/fidelity.ts             @systemslibrarian

# The build gates that enforce what the page says about itself.
/build/                         @systemslibrarian
/scripts/                       @systemslibrarian

# Supply chain and release.
/.github/                       @systemslibrarian
/package.json                   @systemslibrarian
/package-lock.json              @systemslibrarian
/.nvmrc                         @systemslibrarian

# Assurance documentation.
/SECURITY.md                    @systemslibrarian
/THREAT-MODEL.md                @systemslibrarian
/KNOWN-LIMITATIONS.md           @systemslibrarian
